Description:

Adds SMTPUTF8 (RFC 6531) support.  lmtpd accepts UTF-8 envelope addresses
when the client requests SMTPUTF8, including plus-addresses that name a
folder in UTF-8.  Outgoing mail (Sieve redirect and vacation, JMAP
EmailSubmission, iMIP) uses SMTPUTF8 when the relay supports it, and
otherwise sends internationalized domains as A-labels.  A message for a
non-ASCII local-part is refused when the relay doesn't support SMTPUTF8.
JMAP advertises "smtputf8" in submissionExtensions when the relay does.


Documentation:

docsrc/rfc-support.rst, and the imapd.conf options listed below.


Config changes:

lmtpd advertises SMTPUTF8 exactly when imapd advertises UTF8=ACCEPT: when
both munge8bit and reject8bit are disabled.  lmtp_strict_rfc2821 no longer
applies to SMTPUTF8 transactions.  httpd logs
jmap.submission.smtputf8.mismatch when the outbound relay's SMTPUTF8
support differs from lmtpd's.

Changed: lmtp_strict_rfc2821, munge8bit, reject8bit


Upgrade instructions:

None.  With the default munge8bit enabled, lmtpd behaves as before.


